      "text": "The short-term reversal factor is long the two low-prior-return portfolios and short the two high-prior-return portfolios, averaged across size: ST_Rev = \u00bd(SMALL LoPRIOR + BIG LoPRIOR) \u2212 \u00bd(SMALL HiPRIOR + BIG HiPRIOR). The script parses only the first (value-weighted) table, treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, and drops any month where a needed portfolio is missing. I have not run it against the full file.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport math\nimport re\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\n\nMISSING_VALUES = (-99.99, -999.0)\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s.strip())\n\n\ndef is_missing(x):\n    if x is None or math.isnan(x):\n        return True\n    for m in MISSING_VALUES:\n        if abs(x - m) < 1e-9:\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef to_float(s):\n    try:\n        return float(s.strip())\n    except (ValueError, AttributeError):\n        return float(\"nan\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    header = None\n    col = {}\n    data = []  # list of (yyyymm, list of floats)\n    started = False\n\n    with open(INPUT, newline=\"\") as f:\n        reader = csv.reader(f)\n        for parts in reader:\n            if not parts or all(p.strip() == \"\" for p in parts):\n                if started:\n                    break  # end of first table block\n                continue\n            first = parts[0].strip()\n            if header is None:\n                names = [norm(p) for p in parts]\n                if \"SMALL LoPRIOR\" in names:\n                    header = names\n                    for i, nm in enumerate(names):\n                        col[nm] = i\n                continue\n            if re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", first):\n                started = True\n                data.append((int(first), parts))\n            else:\n                if started:\n                    break  # first table ended; ignore subsequent sections\n\n    if header is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not locate value-weighted header row\")\n\n    need = [\"SMALL LoPRIOR\", \"BIG LoPRIOR\", \"SMALL HiPRIOR\", \"BIG HiPRIOR\"]\n    for nm in need:\n        if nm not in col:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Missing column {nm}\")\n\n    results = []\n    for ym, parts in data:\n        vals = {}\n        for nm in need:\n            idx = col[nm]\n            v = to_float(parts[idx]) if idx < len(parts) else float(\"nan\")\n            vals[nm] = float(\"nan\") if is_missing(v) else v\n        if any(math.isnan(vals[nm]) for nm in need):\n            continue\n        st = 0.5 * (vals[\"SMALL LoPRIOR\"] + vals[\"BIG LoPRIOR\"]) \\\n            - 0.5 * (vals[\"SMALL HiPRIOR\"] + vals[\"BIG HiPRIOR\"])\n        results.append((ym, st))\n\n    results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    with open(OUTPUT, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for ym, v in results:\n            w.writerow([ym, repr(float(v))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
